&lt;p&gt;Yahoo supports authenticator-app verification for accounts that meet the required configuration.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The authenticator generates a temporary code that can be used as the second authentication step.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Users should protect the device containing the authenticator.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Yahoo App Verification&lt;br&gt;
Yahoo can also use push notifications through supported Yahoo applications.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A login attempt may require the user to approve the request from a trusted device.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Unexpected approval requests should never be accepted.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Security Keys&lt;br&gt;
A security key is a physical authentication device associated with the account.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Yahoo states that a security key can provide an additional verification step after entering the password.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Users should store security keys securely and maintain appropriate recovery options.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Benefits of Yahoo Accounts with 2FA&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Additional Account Protection
2FA provides another barrier against unauthorized access.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Even if a password is exposed, the attacker may still need the additional verification method.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Better Protection for Email
A Yahoo Mail account can contain:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;• Personal conversations&lt;br&gt;
• Business messages&lt;br&gt;
• Receipts&lt;br&gt;
• Notifications&lt;br&gt;
• Documents&lt;br&gt;
• Contact information&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Additional account protection can help reduce unauthorized access to these resources.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improved Login Awareness
2FA can make users more aware of unexpected login attempts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Users should pay attention to verification requests they did not initiate.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Strong Password Practices&lt;br&gt;
2FA is most effective when combined with a strong password.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A good password should be:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;• Long&lt;br&gt;
• Unique&lt;br&gt;
• Difficult to guess&lt;br&gt;
• Not reused on other services&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Avoid passwords based on easily available information such as names, birthdays, or simple number sequences.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Yahoo also recommends using a strong password as part of its account-security guidance.&lt;/p&gt;

