&lt;p&gt;Important conversations should be retained and organized.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Users can create a simple system for:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;• Personal communication&lt;br&gt;
• Work messages&lt;br&gt;
• Receipts&lt;br&gt;
• Notifications&lt;br&gt;
• Projects&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This makes important information easier to find later.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Search Old Messages&lt;br&gt;
Search functionality can help locate older conversations.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Users may search using information such as:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;• Keywords&lt;br&gt;
• Sender&lt;br&gt;
• Subject&lt;br&gt;
• Dates&lt;br&gt;
• Message content&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A good search strategy can save time when managing a large mailbox.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Yahoo App Passwords&lt;br&gt;
Some third-party applications may require an app password when accessing Yahoo Mail.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Yahoo explains that app passwords can provide secure access for supported third-party applications without sharing the main Yahoo password.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;App passwords should be treated as sensitive credentials.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Managing App Passwords&lt;br&gt;
Users should:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;• Create app passwords only when necessary&lt;br&gt;
• Never share them publicly&lt;br&gt;
• Remove credentials that are no longer needed&lt;br&gt;
• Review unfamiliar app passwords&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Yahoo specifically recommends deleting app passwords that users do not recognize.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Yahoo Accounts on Different Devices&lt;br&gt;
Users may access Yahoo Mail through:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;• Desktop computers&lt;br&gt;
• Laptops&lt;br&gt;
• Smartphones&lt;br&gt;
• Tablets&lt;br&gt;
• Supported email applications&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When using a new device, Yahoo may request additional verification if the sign-in appears unusual.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Public and Shared Computers&lt;br&gt;
Users should be particularly careful when accessing Yahoo Mail from shared devices.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Recommended practices include:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;• Avoid saving passwords&lt;br&gt;
• Sign out after use&lt;br&gt;
• Do not save authentication information&lt;br&gt;
• Avoid accessing sensitive accounts on untrusted devices&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Yahoo recommends signing out from public computers after use.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Common Yahoo Account Problems&lt;br&gt;
Forgotten Password&lt;br&gt;
Users who forget their password should use Yahoo's official Sign-in Helper and available recovery methods.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Yahoo recommends using recovery phone or email information to regain access.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Lost 2FA Device&lt;br&gt;
Losing access to a phone, authenticator, or security key can make account access more difficult.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For this reason, users should maintain appropriate recovery methods and keep recovery information current.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Unrecognized Login&lt;br&gt;
If an unfamiliar login appears, users should review account activity and security settings.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Possible steps include:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;• Change the password&lt;br&gt;
• Review recovery information&lt;br&gt;
• Check authentication methods&lt;br&gt;
• Remove unfamiliar app passwords&lt;br&gt;
• Review account settings&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Signs of a Compromised Yahoo Account&lt;br&gt;
